.TH COW 1
.SH NAME
cow, spots \- run a command on a copy of this directory, and show what it changed
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cow
.I dir
.I cmd
[
.I arg ...
]
.PP
.B spots
.I dir
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Cow
runs
.I cmd
in a new name space where
.IR cowfs (4)
serves the current directory, with every change kept in
.IR dir ,
so that the real files do not change.
.I Dir
may be relative to the current directory;
.I cow
makes it if it does not exist.
.I Cow
refuses a
.I dir
that holds anything, or one inside the current directory.
The command's standard output and error are its own:
.I cow
prints only its own errors.
It keeps the changes whatever the command's status, and exits with that status.
.PP
.I Cow
serves only the current directory and what lies below it.
A command that changes to a directory outside it, or that names a file there, works on the real
files.
.PP
.I Spots
prints the changes kept in
.I dir
as a patch for the current directory, which must be the one
.I cow
ran in.
For each file that the command made, removed, or changed, it prints Git's header,
.BI "diff --git a/" path " b/" path \f1,
then
.B new file mode
or
.B deleted file mode
for a file the command made or removed,
or
.B old mode
and
.B new mode
when the execute bit changed,
and then the unified diff,
against
.B /dev/null
for a file made or removed.
A mode is
.B 100755
when the owner may execute the file, and
.B 100644
otherwise.
The header alone shows an empty file made or removed.
A file changed and then changed back, or made and then removed, does not appear, and
directories appear only through their files.
A rename shows as the old name's removal and the new name's creation.
.I Spots
leaves out Git's
.B index
line, so
.B patch -p1
and
.B git apply
both take its output.
.PP
.IR Cowfs
notes the SHA-1 of each file of the real tree as it copies it;
.I spots
warns of a file whose text has changed since then, as applying its patch would undo that change.
.SH EXAMPLES
Work in a shell, keeping its changes apart, then save them as a patch:
.IP
.EX
cow /tmp/e rc
spots /tmp/e >/tmp/e.patch
.EE
.SH SOURCE
plan9web's
.B rc/bin/cow
and
.B rc/bin/spots
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR diff (1),
.IR cowfs (4)
.SH BUGS
.I Spots
compares the files with APE's
.IR diff ,
which marks no missing newline at the end of a file;
a patch of such a file adds one.
A changed binary file shows as Git's
.B Binary files
line, which no patch applies.
